---
title: Hex reverse
tags: tools
heading: "Reverse hex"
summary: >-
    Reverses the bits in each byte or nibble, or the order of the bytes, which isn't the same as reversing the whole string.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% from "macros/delimiter.njk" import delimiter %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Reversing the whole string turns <code class="tool-example">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> [Hello] into <code class="tool-example">f6 c6 c6 56 84</code>. These reverse it in other ways:</p>
    <dl>
        <dt>Reverse bytes</dt>
        <dd>Reverses the order of the bits within each byte, so <code class="tool-example">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">84 56 c6 c6 f6</code></dd>
        <dt>Reverse byte order</dt>
        <dd>While it sounds similar, byte order is a little different: this reverses the order of the bytes in the string, so <code class="tool-example">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">6f 6c 6c 65 48</code></dd>
        <dt>Reverse nibbles</dt>
        <dd>Reverses the bits within each nibble (4 bits) of every byte. It's the same as converting the hex to binary, reversing the bits in each nibble, then converting it back to hex: <code class="tool-example">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">21 6A 36 36 F6</code></dd>
    </dl>
    <p>Your hex can use any of the usual delimiters between bytes (spaces, hyphens, colons, commas, semicolons, new lines, \x, 0x or %), or none, and they can be mixed. The delimiter dropdown chooses how the result is written.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Reverse hex", placeholder = "Example: 48 65 6c 6c 6f", actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Reverse" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Type"><span class="visually-hidden">What to </span>Reverse</label>
    <select class="form-select" id="{{ filename }}Type" autocomplete="off">
        <option value="bytes" selected="">Bytes</option>
        <option value="byte-order">Byte order</option>
        <option value="nibbles">Nibbles</option>
    </select>
</div>
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Delimiter"><span class="visually-hidden">Hex </span>Delimiter</label>
    {{ delimiter(filename) }}
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
